  Absolutely.  But you can use either method of lujvo formation to get both
meanings.  It's just whether you want to add a gau part to a non-agential
word to make it agential, or use zi'o (or just leave it blank, zo'e'ing it)
to make an agential work into a non-agential one.  Personal preference
*shrug*  If (for example) "lerganzu" means something like "g1 spells word
l3 as g3=3Dl1 in language/by rules g4=3Dl2" you can ask "ma te lerganzu zo
barda" and receive back an answer of "me'o by ce'o abu ce'o ry ce'o dy ce'o
abu" or "me'o by ce'o ibu ce'o gy go'i fi mi lo ka tolmencre se ra'a mi"
    --gejsypa


